 "data_read": "No intraday bar, daily price or implied- or historical-vol value dated 2020-01-01 or later has been read for this work. The calibration's bar loader refuses every month after 2019-12, so no 2020 bar file was opened. The daily price and IV/HV files hold one JSON document per ticker; they are parsed whole, as the research round's loaders parse them, and cut at 2019-12-31 before any value is used (the lab's replay in the calibration gets the cut rows too), so nothing dated 2020 or later entered a computation, a printout or this record. Their sha256 is taken over the files' bytes. The tests use synthetic data only.",
 "check_reads": "The check opens no intraday bar month after 2023-12: its bar loader refuses later months. The overlays' own daily rows and the IV/HV series are cut at 2023-12-31. The daily price rows go to lab.replay, and to the overlays' stock-day pass that must judge eligibility as the lab does, uncut, exactly as lab.run passed them for EXT-FADE.v1's logged check, because the reproduction of that check must be exact. There the lab's printing-error test (intraday_replay.bad_rows) judges a row with the next session's open, so the eligibility of the last 2023 session (2023-12-29) reads the 2024-01-02 open. The daily and IV/HV files are parsed whole before they are cut, and their sha256 covers the whole files.",
 "code_checks": "The runner refuses unless the module on disk is the one the process imported (MODULE_CHANGED_SINCE_IMPORT) and that is the registered one, and likewise the runner as it started (RUNNER_CHANGED_SINCE_IMPORT) and the lab (LAB_CODE_CHANGED_SINCE_IMPORT). The module's hash as imported is written into each log entry.",
 "run_order": [
